<article class="env-lemma" id="0AFS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AFS">Lemma <span data-tag="0AFS">10.110.6</span>.</a> A Noetherian local ring $R$ is a regular local ring if and only if it has finite global dimension. In this case $R_{\mathfrak p}$ is a regular local ring for all primes $\mathfrak p$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Propositions <a href="/tag/00OC" data-tag="00OC">10.110.5</a> and <a href="/tag/00O7" data-tag="00O7">10.110.1</a> we see that a Noetherian local ring is a regular local ring if and only if it has finite global dimension. Furthermore, any localization $R_{\mathfrak p}$ has finite global dimension, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00O8" data-tag="00O8">10.109.13</a>, and hence is a regular local ring. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>